9de|n|A block or clay tempered with water, sand, etc., molded into a regular form, usually rectangular, and sun-dried, or burnt in a kiln, or in a heap or stack called a clamp. ; Bricks, collectively, as designating that kind of material; as, a load of brick; a thousand of brick. ; Any oblong rectangular mass; as, a brick of maple sugar; a penny brick (of bread). ; A good fellow; a merry person; as, you 're a brick.	a:16pq,82,1~16pq,82,1	v:16pq,82,1~16pq,82,1	V:1vrb,103,5~1vrb,103,5	n:16pq,105,5;1m4i,77,30~1m4i,77,30;16pq,105,5	N:1hhv,23,2~1hhv,23,2
