9h9|a|Wide; extend in breadth, or from side to side; -- opposed to narrow; as, a broad street, a broad table; an inch broad. ; Extending far and wide; extensive; vast; as, the broad expanse of ocean. ; Extended, in the sense of diffused; open; clear; full. ; Fig.: Having a large measure of any thing or quality; not limited; not restrained; -- applied to any subject, and retaining the literal idea more or less clearly, the precise meaning depending largely on the substantive. ; Comprehensive; liberal; enlarged. ; Plain; evident; as, a broad hint. ; Free; unrestrained; unconfined. ; Characterized by breadth. See Breadth. ; Cross; coarse; indelicate; as, a broad compliment; a broad joke; broad humor. ; Strongly marked; as, a broad Scotch accent.	j:kjf,109,12;1yby,73,6;bfn,58,4;bfq,53,5;5kl,49,5;1piv,48,9;1sn,43,3;15mk,36,7;29dh,30,4;1v7h,27,5;13cv,27,3;4j6,24,5;1p0j,14,29;nmi,14,1;1p0v,12,11~1p0j,14,29;kjf,109,12;1p0v,12,11;1piv,48,9;3fx,2,8;15mk,36,7;1yby,73,6;4j6,24,5;5kl,49,5;bfq,53,5;1v7h,27,5;29dh,30,4;bfn,58,4;13cv,27,3;1sn,43,3	e:1gk0,76,16;24mq,64,315;11pm,58,4;2109,53,5;rbq,44,7;1xtf,42,8;297h,37,64;1pnb,20,7;1p6j,18,5;1mvc,18,4~24mq,64,315;297h,37,64;1gk0,76,16;1xtf,42,8;1pnb,20,7;rbq,44,7;1p6j,18,5;2109,53,5;11pm,58,4;1mvc,18,4
